Description: Station: probe the audio header off the probe bytes
 The probe used to hand the fetched bytes to the legacy media extractor
 to learn the stream's format. media2's BMediaFile opens an entry_ref or
 a BUrl only, so ProbeBuffer parses the MPEG audio (Layer III) or ADTS
 frame header of the probe bytes itself and fills sample rate, channels,
 bitrate, encoding and frame size from it -- a header read, not a
 decoder. The probe window grows from 4 KiB to 64 KiB so an ID3v2 tag
 does not hide the first frame; stations whose format stays unknown rely
 on the Ice-Audio-Info response header, as they already did.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
